{"content":[{"c":["BETH-JESHIMOTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City assigned to Reuben’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.20","r":"Josh.13.20","rawR":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.20","value":"Josh.13.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:20"},"), later described as a Moabite town (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.25.9","r":"Ezek.25.9","rawR":"Ezek.25.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.25.9","value":"Ezek.25.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 25:9"},"). Prior to Israel’s conquest of the Promised Land, they made camp along the Jordan from Beth-jeshimoth to Abel-shittim (",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.49","r":"Num.33.49","rawR":"Num.33.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.49","value":"Num.33.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 33:49"},"). The city is usually identified with Tell el-Azeimeh."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BethJeshimoth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 13:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.20","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.20","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.20"},{"anchorText":"Ez 25:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.25.9","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.25.9","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.25.9"},{"anchorText":"Nm 33:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.49","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.49","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.49"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7f72b3fddd630f9a3ca1bd3c6f0c344ac40e999445a0f28bfda3bc0df53a348c","sourceItemName":"BethJeshimoth","sourceItemOrder":257